      ],
      "title": "⏰ Expected Time to Block",
      "description": "Statistical average time until you find a block based on your current hashrate and network difficulty.\n\n• Formula: ETB = (difficulty × 2³²) / hashrate\n• This is an AVERAGE - you could find a block sooner or later\n• Updates in real-time as hashrate and difficulty change\n\nExample: With 13.8 TH/s at 750B difficulty ≈ 27 days\n\nNote: Solo mining is a lottery - this number represents the statistical expectation over many attempts.",
      "type": "stat"
    },
